While the battle pass did have a set amount for [[Hardcore Mode|Hardcore]] mode, that being {{DuckyEggs|800}} which when divided by total waves would make it give {{DuckyEggs|16}}, this did not work and [[Hardcore Mode|Hardcore]] mode instead gave nothing.

In total, it took {{DuckyEggs|27,080}} to complete the battle pass. The battle pass had two tracks, the regular track could have been obtained for free and the premium track was purchasable for {{Robux|499}}. During the Memorial Day 2025 Sale, it had a cost of {{Robux|424}}.

While the battle pass could have all its Levels skipped with one purchase, this was not advised, as while the prices for skipping single Levels had been decreased since [[Operation I.C.E Event]], prices for skipping all Levels had remained unchanged. Most noticeably, Level 40 costed {{Robux|210}} to skip, however, skipping all Levels, which should have an identical cost, costed {{Robux|460}} instead, which is higher by {{Robux|250}}. In total, this meant the player saved {{Robux|1,390}} by purchasing every Level individually. Additionally, as Level 22 required the same amount of currency as Level 21, it would get unlocked after the player purchases Level 21. While Level 22 cost was accounted for in skipping all Levels, it could be entirely skipped by buying individual Levels, saving a total of {{Robux|1,464}}.

Certain items like [[High Grade Crate]]s are given out multiple times. In total, the '''Ducky Revenge Battle Pass''' gives out {{Coins|4,200}}, {{Exp|2,550}}, {{TimeScaleTicket|12}}, 12 [[Ducky Squad]]s, 4 [[High Grade Crate]]s, 2 [[Premium Crate]]s, {{SpinTicket|15}}, 13 [[Easter Egg]]s and 9 [[Molten Monster (Consumable)|Molten Monsters]].

